    "task_id": "task_05_digital_clock",
    "title": "Digital Clock (HH:MM:SS)",
    "description": "Build a digital clock using a 555 timer IC and 6 seven-segment displays in HH:MM:SS format. The student must demonstrate ALL five behaviours: (1) Seconds counting — the display visibly counts upward and seconds digits roll over from 59 back to 00; (2) Minutes auto-increment — after seconds roll over at 60 the minutes value increases by 1; (3) Hours button — pressing the hours button increments the hours digit and it resets after reaching 12; (4) Minutes button — pressing the minutes button manually increments minutes resetting after 60; (5) Reset button — pressing reset zeroes the seconds back to 00. A submission is accepted only if all five behaviours are clearly demonstrated and verbally explained.",
    "components": {
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        {
